    "result_text": "Both tests pass. Let me verify the full picture is clean \u2014 the build succeeded and both `@core` tests are green.\n\nThe change is complete and verified end-to-end. Here's what I implemented as a full-stack, additive change:\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V1__clients.sql`)\n- New Flyway migration creating the `client` table (`id` identity, `name`, `email`).\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST + Spring beans)\n- `Client` JPA entity + `ClientRepository` (with `findAllByOrderByIdAsc` for stable ordering).\n- `GET /api/clients` \u2192 `ClientsGet` logic + `clients.GET.yml` (lists clients).\n- `POST /api/clients` \u2192 `ClientsPost` logic + `clients.POST.yml`, taking a `@RequestBody NewClient`, saving via the repository, and recording a `CLIENT_CREATED \u2026` line through the `Audit` service.\n- Extended `TestSupportController` so `/__test__/reset` truncates `client` with `RESTART IDENTITY` and `/__test__/seed` inserts clients by their fixture ids via `JdbcTemplate`.\n\n**Front-end** (all new files, nothing existing edited)\n- `features/clients/nav.slot.tsx` \u2014 the `nav-clients` link filling the `AppNav` slot.\n- `features/clients/ClientsPage.tsx` \u2014 the list (`clients-table`, `client-row-<id>`, `client-name`, `client-email`), the empty state (`clients-empty`), and the add form (`client-form-name`, `client-form-email`, `client-form-submit`). Server data via `useQuery(['clients'])`; create via `useMutation` + `invalidateQueries`.\n- `routes/clients.index.tsx` \u2014 the `/clients` page.\n\nVerification: `cd src/main/frontend && npm run typecheck` passes, and `bin/e2e` builds, boots, and runs the spec green:\n\n```\n\u2713 clients \u203a lists seeded clients\n\u2713 clients \u203a creates a client\n2 passed\n```\n\nI stayed within the pinned files (didn't touch `bin/*`, `CLAUDE.md`, the shared front-end mechanism, or the spec), and the data-testids match the spec's contract exactly.",
